<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakhstan parliament passes 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Kazakhstan parliament passes 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's parliament has passed a 1997 budget calling for a deficit of 3.16 percent of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>A joint session of both houses of parliament on Wednesday approved a budget providing for 177.8 billion tenge of revenues, 199.3 billion tenge of spending, and net new borrowing of 33.4 billion tenge.</p>
<p>The deficit of 54.9 billion tenge will be covered by domestic and foreign borrowing.</p>
<p>The final version of the budget has not yet been published, but parliament officials said the revenue and spending figures would not be changed.</p>
<p>($1 = 73.69 tenge)</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
